{"task_id": "HumanEval/30", "solution": "def get_positive(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return only positive numbers in the list.\n    >>> get_positive([-1, 2, -4, 5, 6])\n    [2, 5, 6]\n    >>> get_positive([5, 3, -5, 2, -3, 3, 9, 0, 123, 1, -10])\n    [5, 3, 2, 3, 9, 0, 123, 1]\n    \"\"\"\n    return [x for x in l if x > 0]"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/31", "solution": "import math\ndef is_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an integer n is a prime number.\n    It uses an optimized trial division algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return False\n    if n == 2 or n == 3:\n        return True\n\n    if n % 2 == 0 or n % 3 == 0:\n        return False\n\n    i = 5\n    while i * i <= n:\n        if n % i == 0 or n % (i + 2) == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 6\n\n    return True"}
