{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the Fib4 sequence iteratively.\n    It uses constant space by keeping track of the last four terms.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize variables with fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n    f_n_minus_4 = 0\n    f_n_minus_3 = 0\n    f_n_minus_2 = 2\n    f_n_minus_1 = 0\n\n    # Iterate from the 4th term up to n\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        current_fib = f_n_minus_1 + f_n_minus_2 + f_n_minus_3 + f_n_minus_4\n        # Update the sequence values\n        f_n_minus_4, f_n_minus_3, f_n_minus_2, f_n_minus_1 = f_n_minus_3, f_n_minus_2, f_n_minus_1, current_fib\n        \n    return f_n_minus_1"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "def median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    if not l:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty\")\n\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # Odd number of elements: return the middle element.\n        middle_index = n // 2\n        return sorted_l[middle_index]\n    else:\n        # Even number of elements: return the average of the two middle elements.\n        middle_right_index = n // 2\n        middle_left_index = middle_right_index - 1\n        return (sorted_l[middle_left_index] + sorted_l[middle_right_index]) / 2"}
