{"task_id": "HumanEval/61", "solution": "def correct_bracketing(brackets: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a string of '(' and ')' has correct bracketing.\n\n    Every opening bracket must have a corresponding closing bracket, and they\n    must be correctly nested.\n    \"\"\"\n    balance = 0\n    for char in brackets:\n        if char == '(':\n            balance += 1\n        elif char == ')':\n            balance -= 1\n        \n        # If balance ever drops below zero, it means a closing bracket appeared\n        # without a matching opening bracket before it.\n        if balance < 0:\n            return False\n            \n    # For correct bracketing, the final balance must be exactly zero.\n    # A positive balance means unmatched opening brackets.\n    return balance == 0"}
