{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "def circular_shift(x, shift):\n    \"\"\"Performs a circular right shift on an integer's digits, returning a string.\n    Handles negative signs and reversal if shift exceeds digit count.\"\"\"\n    is_negative = (x < 0)\n    s = str(abs(x))\n    n = len(s)\n\n    # This handles an unlikely edge case for integer input where n could be 0, though str(0) is \"0\".\n    if n == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    # If shift is greater than digit count, reverse the digits.\n    if shift > n:\n        result_s = s[::-1]\n    else:\n        # Calculates the effective shift amount for circular rotation.\n        effective_shift = shift % n\n\n        # If effective shift is zero, no change is needed.\n        if effective_shift == 0:\n            result_s = s\n        else:\n            # Performs the actual circular right shift.\n            result_s = s[-effective_shift:] + s[:-effective_shift]\n\n    # Reapplies the original sign if necessary.\n    if is_negative:\n        return \"-\" + result_s\n    else:\n        return result_s"}
