{"task_id": "HumanEval/69", "solution": "from collections import Counter\ndef search(lst):\n    # Count frequencies of all numbers in the list.\n    freq_map = Counter(lst)\n\n    # Initialize the result variable to -1 to handle cases where no such integer exists.\n    max_k = -1\n\n    # Iterate through the unique numbers and their frequencies.\n    for k, freq in freq_map.items():\n        # Check if the frequency of k is greater than or equal to k itself.\n        if freq >= k:\n            # If the condition is met, update max_k with the greater value.\n            max_k = max(max_k, k)\n            \n    # Return the greatest integer found, or -1.\n    return max_k"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/70", "solution": "def strange_sort_list(lst):\n    '''\n    Given list of integers, return list in strange order.\n    Strange sorting, is when you start with the minimum value,\n    then maximum of the remaining integers, then minimum and so on.\n    '''\n    if not lst:\n        return []\n\n    # Sort the input list, making it easy to pick minimum and maximum of remaining elements.\n    sorted_lst = sorted(lst)\n\n    result = []\n    \n    # Initialize two pointers, one at the beginning and one at the end of the sorted list.\n    left_ptr = 0\n    right_ptr = len(sorted_lst) - 1\n    \n    # Use a boolean flag to alternate between picking the minimum and maximum value, starting with minimum.\n    is_min_turn = True \n\n    # Iterate while the left pointer has not crossed the right pointer.\n    while left_ptr <= right_ptr:\n        if is_min_turn:\n            # If it's the turn to pick a minimum, append the element at the left pointer and move the pointer right.\n            result.append(sorted_lst[left_ptr])\n            left_ptr += 1\n        else:\n            # If it's the turn to pick a maximum, append the element at the right pointer and move the pointer left.\n            result.append(sorted_lst[right_ptr])\n            right_ptr -= 1\n        \n        # Toggle the flag for the next iteration.\n        is_min_turn = not is_min_turn\n\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/71", "solution": "import math\ndef triangle_area(a, b, c):\n    '''\n    Calculates the area of a triangle given its three side lengths.\n    Returns the area rounded to two decimal places, or -1 if the sides do not form a valid triangle.\n    '''\n    if a <= 0 or b <= 0 or c <= 0:\n        return -1\n\n    if not (a + b > c and a + c > b and b + c > a):\n        return -1\n\n    s = (a + b + c) / 2\n    area = math.sqrt(s * (s - a) * (s - b) * (s - c))\n\n    return round(area, 2)"}
